    <section class="section"><div class="container article"><p class="answer-block"><strong>In brief:</strong> Perth Coastal Gardens helps homeowners enquire about garden rejuvenation, sandy-soil improvement, waterwise landscaping and reticulation across Perth’s northern coastal corridor. The focus is established gardens affected by fast-draining sand, dry summers, strong sun and varying coastal exposure.</p><p>Two properties in neighbouring suburbs can need very different solutions. A sheltered Joondalup courtyard may retain moisture and support a wider planting palette, while a west-facing Mullaloo frontage may experience salt-laden wind, intense afternoon heat and rapid drying. Useful advice begins with the conditions around the home rather than the suburb name alone.</p></div></section>
